The increasing demand for high-quality digital imaging is accelerating the adoption of backside-illuminated (BSI) CMOS image sensors across smartphones, automotive cameras, industrial vision systems and medical imaging equipment. As camera systems are expected to deliver better low-light performance, higher resolution and more reliable image capture, BSI technology is becoming increasingly important in modern image-sensor design.

According to Semiconductor Insight, the global BSI CMOS Image Sensor Market was valued at USD 8.98 billion in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 25.81 billion by 2034, expanding at a CAGR of 12.4% during the 2026–2034 forecast period. Asia Pacific held the largest regional position in the report's coverage.

BSI CMOS image sensors position the light-sensitive photodiode layer behind much of the metal interconnect structure, reducing obstruction to incoming light. This architecture can improve photon collection and support better sensitivity in compact imaging devices.

